KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ forwarding-reference pack forwards correctly: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Expanding a forwarding-reference parameter pack `A&&... a` in a call-argument
pattern `f(static_cast<A&&>(a)...)` does not substitute the type pack A in
lockstep, so the forwarded arguments are wrong and the call computes the wrong
result (assertion 1 currently FAILS).  Flip to CORE once forwarding-reference
parameter-pack pattern expansion is implemented.  This is the body of the
variadic std::__invoke and the remaining blocker for multi-argument
std::function.
